Package: tind-graphics
Version: 0.1.5
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Morten <morten@servr.no>
Section: metapackages
Priority: optional
Depends: curl, gnupg, dkms, mokutil, linux-headers-amd64, nvidia-driver, nvidia-kernel-dkms, nvidia-vulkan-icd, nvidia-detect, mesa-vulkan-drivers, libgl1-mesa-dri, mesa-va-drivers, mesa-vdpau-drivers, firmware-amd-graphics, vulkan-tools, mesa-utils, pciutils
Recommends: nvidia-settings, intel-media-va-driver-non-free
Installed-Size: 4
Description: Tind graphics: NVIDIA, Mesa, Vulkan and video drivers
 NVIDIA proprietary driver (DKMS, rebuilt automatically for new kernels),
 Mesa Vulkan and VA-API for AMD and Intel, AMD graphics firmware.
 Games and developer tools are separate: see tind-extras. A boot-time check falls back to the open nouveau driver
 when an NVIDIA card is too old for the packaged driver.
 On the first boot of an installed system with internet, a card of the RTX 20 / GTX 16 generation or newer is
 moved to NVIDIA's own Debian repository (current driver branch); older cards stay on Debian's driver. Any failure
 leaves the packaged driver in place.
